    "body": "Yeah, and the y-position check could work for fish and perhaps other shells (won't work for zsh/bash on clear since the prompt is not re-evaluated on clear, iirc).\r\n\r\nThe way pwsh on mac queries the position [seems quite involved](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/8f5364695b107f37af899aba3ad1b9f98d577c33/src/libraries/System.Console/src/System/ConsolePal.Unix.cs#L437-L672), it might be an idea to query the cursor position from rust on nix based machines in a similar way.\r\n\r\nCmd would probably use win32 the same as pwsh/powershell on windows I think.\r\nMany ideas 🤔 ",
